**Module 8 – Lesson 2: AI/ML on AWS**

Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Machine Learning (ML) are used by businesses worldwide to solve real-world problems and improve decision-making. Amazon itself uses ML models in its e-commerce recommendation engine, fulfillment center optimization, and many other business operations. Machine Learning can be used for predicting trends, making decisions, and detecting anomalies. For example, ML models can predict future stock prices, route customer calls to the correct department based on voice requests, and identify suspicious banking transactions or fraud.

AWS provides AI and ML solutions through the AWS AI/ML Stack, which consists of three tiers. The first tier is AWS AI Services, which provides pre-built and pre-trained AI models. These services are ready to use without requiring ML knowledge. Examples include Amazon Polly for converting text into speech and Amazon Comprehend for text analysis and sentiment analysis.

The second tier is AWS ML Services, where businesses can create their own machine learning models. The primary service is Amazon SageMaker AI. SageMaker helps users build, train, deploy, monitor, debug, and manage machine learning models using fully managed AWS infrastructure. It also provides tools for experiment tracking, data visualization, and model monitoring in one environment.

The third tier is ML Frameworks and Infrastructure, which is the most customizable approach. Businesses can build highly specialized machine learning solutions using AWS infrastructure, purpose-built AI chips, and popular machine learning frameworks. These solutions can run on ML-optimized Amazon EC2 instances for maximum flexibility and control.

